On Fri, Nov 14, 2014 at 4:19 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

> Is there a simple algorithm for detecting valid brivla in general (without
> specifying whether they are fu'ivla, gismu of lujvo) ?
>
> I mean such algorithm is supposed to be simpler than the current brivlakle
> detection algorithm in the current PEG.
>

No, because of the slinku'i rule. The slinku'i rule means you need to
examine the rafsi structure of your candidate form anyway, so determining
whether it's a gismu, lujvo or fu'ivla is not much more complicated than
determining whether it's a valid brivla. You can't avoid rafsi
unfortunately.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

